\begin_layout Standard

\backslash
section{Spectral finite element framework}
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\backslash
label{Sec:FEM}
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We now describe the spectral finite-element framework employed in SPARC-atomSFE.
 The finite-element method is chosen for its systematic improvability,
 support for high-order approximations,
 and flexibility in accommodating adaptive grids,
 properties that together yield an accurate and accurate scheme in the present context.
 Here,
 the term 
\backslash
emph{spectral} refers to the use of high-order polynomial approximations in conjunction with appropriately chosen quadrature rules,
 consistent with its usage in the finite-element literature~
\backslash
cite{PATERA1984468}.
 The framework,
 schematically illustrated in Fig.~
\backslash
ref{Fig:FEM},
 is described in detail next.
 
\end_layout

