\begin_layout Standard
SPARC-atomSFE supports both all-electron and pseudopotential calculations,
 with the latter employing Optimized Norm-Conserving Vanderbilt (ONCV) pseudopotentials~
\backslash
cite{hamann2013optimized} in the 
\backslash
texttt{.psp8} format,
 optionally including nonlinear core corrections.
 The package provides a broad range of exchange-correlation approximations,
 including LDA with Slater exchange and Vosko--Wilk--Nusair~
\backslash
cite{LDA_VWN},
 Perdew--Zunger~
\backslash
cite{perdew1981self},
 or Perdew--Wang~
\backslash
cite{perdew1992accurate} correlation;
 GGA with the Perdew--Burke--Ernzerhof (PBE) functional~
\backslash
cite{perdew1996generalized};
 meta-GGA with the Strongly Constrained and Appropriately Normed (SCAN)~
\backslash
cite{sun2015strongly},
 rSCAN~
\backslash
cite{bartok2019regularized},
 and r$^2$SCAN~
\backslash
cite{r2SCAN} functionals;
 hybrid functionals,
 including PBE0~
\backslash
cite{adamo1999toward} and a generalized PBE0 form with variable exact-exchange mixing;
 Hartree--Fock (HF) theory~
\backslash
cite{Fock1930126};
 and RPA-OEP.
 Charged atoms and fractional occupations are supported across all these cases.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The electronic ground state is obtained using the self-consistent field (SCF) method.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For functionals involving nonlocal exchange-correlation potentials,
 such as HF and PBE0,
 an outer--inner loop structure is employed:
 the outer loop performs a fixed-point iteration with respect to the nonlocal potential operator,
 which is held fixed during each inner loop,
 while the inner loop performs a fixed-point iteration with respect to the electron density.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For RPA-OEP calculations,
 the same outer--inner loop strategy is used,
 with the outer loop performing a fixed-point iteration with respect to the OEP exchange-correlation potential.
 The initial guess for the orbitals in the outer loop is taken from a fully converged 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
PBE calculation or from the first PBE iteration,
 while the initial electron density 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
is obtained from the Thomas-Fermi approximation or from PBE when available.
 Inner-loop convergence is accelerated using the the periodic Pulay mixing scheme~
\backslash
cite{banerjee2016periodic},
 with the option of the RPA dielectric matrix as a preconditioner.
 Direct linear solvers are employed for the Poisson,
 exact exchange,
 and OEP equations.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Direct eigensolvers are used for all functionals except SCAN and r$^2$SCAN,
 for which an iterative eigensolver is employed through Hamiltonian-vector products,
 as this was found to be more stable.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The OEP equation for the local exchange-correlation potential 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
is solved up to an indeterminate constant.
 The RPA-OEP potential is therefore 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
shifted by a constant to match $-1/r$ at a specified distance 
\backslash
cite{vacondiopaper},
 e.g.,
 $9$~bohr in 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
practice,
 and the potential beyond this distance is set to 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
$-1/r$,
 consistent with the asymptotic decay of the exact exchange potential that 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
dominates at large $r$.
 This correction is applied 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
to avoid numerical instabilities that can manifest as oscillations near the boundary 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
for large domain sizes,
 a consequence of the singular nature of the density response matrix.
